// PARAM: --analysis interval --context call-string --context-depth 1
// Bounding witness for issue #77: a self-recursive procedure called at a
// depth (50) far exceeding the call-string bound (1). cs_route truncates
// every routed context to length <= 1 (cs_route_length,
// Call_String_Context.thy), so fact's own recursive call site produces at
// most 2 distinct call-string contexts (length 0 and length 1) no matter
// how deep the concrete recursion runs -- proved in general for any
// compiled program by compiled_call_strings_finite
// (Call_String_Context_Finite.thy), not just observed here. The CLI
// completes immediately rather than growing one context per recursion
// level, which is exactly the context-explosion #77 is about.
// The check itself stays UNKNOWN, not PROVED: call-string depth bounds
// *context* growth, not interval's own precision loss on an unbounded
// recursive multiplication -- a different, known imprecision (see the
// identical verdict on this same program under plain --analysis interval
// in tests/regression/11-graph-snapshot/known-imprecision/03-recursion.vimp).
void fact(n) {
  if (n < 2) {
    return 1
  } else {
    tmp := fact(n - 1);
    return n * tmp
  }
}
void main() {
  r := fact(50);
  __voblint_check(0 < r) // UNKNOWN
}
